<title>GERMANY: B.U.S 95/96 earnings surged - newsletter.</title>
<headline>B.U.S 95/96 earnings surged - newsletter.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales and earnings at German waste recycling company B.U.S Berzelius Umwelt-Service AG rose sharply in the business year ended September 30 1996, German newsletter Platow-Brief reported late on Friday.</p>
<p>Group earnings rose 50 percent to 24.5 million marks and earnings per share as calculated by the DVFA analysis method rose as much as 125 percent to 90 pfennigs from 40 pfennigs.</p>
<p>Sales rose to 337 million marks from 244 million, Platow said.</p>
<p>The company's dividend is expected to rise to three marks per common share from two marks, the newsletter added.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
